cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data or website, please cite it as below and include the date you retrieved it, because the analysis is updated continuously."
type: dataset
title: "Syria Narrative Tracker: what is being said about Syria online"
authors:
  - name: "Syria Narrative Tracker"
    website: "https://www.syrianpulse.org/"
abstract: "An automatically updated dataset and website following public online discussion about Syria: public posts in Arabic, Kurdish and English from Telegram channels, news feeds, YouTube comments, Reddit and X, grouped by a language model into stories filed under fixed themes, with the tone of people's reactions and of outlet coverage, per theme, per language and per kind of outlet. Individuals' posts are never stored; the data holds analyses and outlet headlines only."
keywords:
  - Syria
  - public opinion
  - narratives
  - social media
  - sentiment
  - Arabic
  - Kurdish
url: "https://www.syrianpulse.org/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Brunopomodoro/syria-narrative-tracker"
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-09-11"
